course: dictionary
lesson: 15850
title: The word uneducated
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Uneducated starts with un-, which means not, as in unhappy. So uneducated means not educated. It describes someone who has had little or no schooling.
explain: «In the past, many children were uneducated because they had to work instead of going to school.» The sentence gives the reason: these children had no chance to learn at school. Today, education is a right, so every child should get the chance to go to school.
explain: Uneducated can also describe speech, writing or guesses that show little knowledge. «An uneducated guess» is a joking phrase, the opposite of «an educated guess». Be careful with people, though. How someone talks is not a sign of schooling, so calling a person uneducated because of their accent or dialect is rude.
fact: Uneducated means having had little or no schooling or education.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so uneducated is the opposite of educated.
fact: Uneducated can describe speech, writing or guesses that show little knowledge.
fact: «An uneducated guess» is a joking phrase, the opposite of «an educated guess».
fact: Accents and dialects are not uneducated, so calling someone uneducated for how they talk is rude and snobbish.
exercise: «In the past, many children were uneducated because they had to work.» What does uneducated mean here? | *Had little or no schooling | Very tired from playing | Very clever and well read | Lost in the town
exercise: What is the joking opposite of «an educated guess»? | An ancient guess | *An uneducated guess | A loud guess
exercise: Ravi's gran has a strong Yorkshire accent. Is her way of talking uneducated? | Yes, because she is old | Yes, because it is different from ours | *No, accents and dialects are not uneducated | Only if she speaks quickly
test: Which word means having had little or no schooling? | Unhappy | Unfair | Educated | *Uneducated
test: What does uneducated suggest in «an uneducated guess»? | Very long | Made with a big smile | *Made with little knowledge | Very kind
exam: Why is it rude to call a person's dialect uneducated? | Because it is a long word | Because dialects are always wrong | Because only teachers may speak | *Because dialects are not uneducated, and calling them so is snobbish
